# Resend API key, used by /api/feedback to send the feedback form's
# submissions by email.
#
# Named PAYRECKON_FEEDBACK_SENDING rather than Resend's own generic
# convention, because that is the name actually configured in Vercel for
# this project. The two must match exactly, in both directions — if this
# is ever renamed, update app/api/feedback/route.ts in the same change, or
# the route silently starts returning "not configured".
#
# This is a real secret: it is read only on the server (no NEXT_PUBLIC_
# prefix), never reaches the browser, and is scoped to sending-only access
# restricted to a specific verified domain in Resend. Whatever domain it is
# scoped to, FEEDBACK_FROM below must be an address on that domain, or every
# send is rejected before it leaves Resend.
#
# Set it in Vercel: Project -> Settings -> Environment Variables. Test on a
# Preview deployment before setting it for Production — a feedback-form
# change is exactly the kind of thing that should prove itself end to end
# on a real deployment before going live.
#
# Without it, /api/feedback returns 503 and the form tells the visitor it
# is not configured, rather than reporting success with nothing sent.
PAYRECKON_FEEDBACK_SENDING=

# Both optional, and FEEDBACK_TO in particular should not be left on its
# hardcoded default without checking. The default destination mailbox is
# the one address this project has actual evidence is real — a different
# address was found to bounce outright on a real send through this exact
# route ("Recipient address rejected: Address does not exist") despite
# having been assumed correct for months. Confirm any destination actually
# receives mail before relying on it; a provider accepting a send proves
# delivery to its own system, not that the mailbox at the far end exists.
FEEDBACK_FROM=
FEEDBACK_TO=
